  "device": "RTX 3050 Laptop GPU 6 GiB; required largest MLP has 5 hidden layers x 512 units",
  "method": "For a fixed-length chronological univariate task, train windows per series are max(0, length - L - 2H + 1). Using only aggregate total values and series count gives the conservative lower bound max(0,total_values - series_count*(L+2H-1)). The lower bound counts all windows, including those with missing targets/features, under train-only mean imputation; the largest architecture hidden-activation storage alone is lower_bound*5*512*4 bytes. This excludes input/target tensors, gradients, parameters, Adam state, validation tensors, and CUDA workspace. Lower-bound activation storage above 6 GiB proves infeasibility; smaller Sunspot route is excluded for only one independent series. These are profile-specific gates, not claims about every possible context length/batch policy.",
  "profiles_note": "Fixed profiles use declared Monash horizon when available, otherwise documented frequency defaults where applicable; context lengths are explicit screen choices. All missing values may be mean-imputed fit on training only, so missingness does not reduce the example count in this resource proof.",
